NAVIGATION
  Web `/account/privacy` has no dedicated value-less `AppRoute` case, and
  `Sources/App` is outside this prompt's allowed files. Following the accepted
  sibling precedent (QuietHours / BrowserNotifications), the page ships as a
  NavigationStack-ready View plus a typed deep-link NavigationDestination
  (`PrivacyLink` + `.privacyDestination()` + `PrivacyRouteRegistration.make()`).
  The `/account/...` first segment already resolves through AppRouteParser to the
  Account side-nav category, so the page is reachable + deep-linkable on the
  macOS/iPad detail column and the iPhone stack without widening the shared enum.

ADAPTIVE / HIG / a11y / units
  - macOS/iPad (regular): each inset region lays its title block + actions side
    by side. iPhone (compact, horizontalSizeClass): stacked. Header copy-link
    likewise. Driven by the @Observable PrivacyPageModel (ADR-004).
  - Materials via TSGlassPanel; tokens-only color/typography (P2). Destructive
    clear via .confirmationDialog (HIG), with the web silence-key contract.
  - VoiceOver labels/traits on header/regions/actions, Dynamic Type, light/dark
    via tokens, >=44pt targets (TSButton). The stored-count uses the catalog's
    plural variation, formatted at the display boundary only.
  - Every visible string via LocalizedStringKey/String(localized:) from
    Localizable.xcstrings with web-aligned key names; zero hardcoded literals.

