# DUPLICATE-SYMBOL NOTE (in-scope correctness)
  The experimental `feature-views/PrivacySection.*` unit already defines
  `PrivacyConsentState`, `InMemoryRecentPagesStore`, `InMemoryConsentStore`, and
  `feature-views/AdvancedSettings.Model.swift` defines `InMemoryConfirmSilenceStore`
  / `UserDefaultsConfirmSilenceStore`. This unit's data-source types were named
  with a distinct `AccountPrivacy*` prefix so the PAGE adds ZERO new collisions
  (a full re-scan of every type this unit declares against Sources/ + TeslaSync/
  + design/ shows no real collision). This both keeps the module honest and
  fixes the `PrivacySection.Previews` "ambiguous PrivacyConsentState" errors that
  an un-prefixed name would have caused.

